XSM simulator for eXpl

Usage 
----------

 ./xsm [ -l <path to library> ] -e <path to program> [--debug]

Note: Paths must be relative


There are four script in this XSM_EXPL FOLDER

script.sh
batch.sh
seg_batch.sh
label_translation/label.sh (it is inside the label_translation folder)


First we run batch.sh or seg_batch.sh based on the context

That is: 
    1. If you are recieving any segmentation fault you can run the seg_batch.sh script to get the file and line no. 
        on which segementation fault occurred.

    2. If you have have no segmentation fault issues then running the batch.sh is fine else if running seg_batch.sh it will show memory leaks 
        because i am not freeing the AST, DimNodes and GST as freeing memory for this program is of no importance as far as the project is concerned.

After that run the script.sh script because after compilation by batch.sh or seg_batch.sh we get the executable file "sol.out" 
which on running will generate the contents to a.xsm file but it will contain Labels like L0,L1,L2 but the xsm compiler will not handle labels which without 
processing will causing error. So to avoid that I have created another folder called label_translation which will contain a lex program label.l that handles 
all labels and translates all the labels present on the (JMP,JZ,JNZ) XSM instruction to the corresponding address values.
This file contains a script label.sh which will generate an executable file named "translator.out" and is automaticaly run by the label.sh script

What the script.sh does is that it will run the sol.out and then runs the label.sh script to translate the labels to corresponding address values
and thus making it usable by the XSM compiler.

Which then can be run using the command

 ./xsm -l library.lib -e a.xsm




